h Argentina, Brazil, and Uruguay splitting several titles.  The 1947 European Champion had been the Soviet Union, but they did not participate in the 1948 Olympics. So, by default, the Americans were still considered the heavy favorites."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The bulk of the United States came from the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/3758"} "University of Kentucky"] ", which won the NCAA Championship in 1948, and would repeat in 1949.  Players from several club teams that had competed in a US Trials were also chosen to make up the final US Olympic basketball team.  Among these was " [:a {:href "/athletes/5679"} "Don Barksdale"] ", the first black man to compete in Olympic basketball.  Barksdale had previously been an AAU champion in the triple jump in 1944, and played club ball for the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/7553"} "Oakland Bittners"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the preliminary rounds, the US had its first close game in Olympic competition, narrowly defeating Argentina 59-57.  However, once thru to the classification matches, they were unmatched, winning the final over France 65-21."] "\n\n" [:p {} "After the Olympics, several of the Kentucky Olympic basketball players, among them " [:a {:href "/athletes/6215"} "Alex Groza"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/5694"} "Ralph Beard"] ", formed a new team in the NBA, the Indianapolis Olympians, which played in the league from 1949-1953."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button300434", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button300434').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Scoring Average"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Disqualifications"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} 